 \"Where was Airways International based?\", \"slot_hint\": \"place\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 83, \"text\": \"Airways International Airways International was an airline based in Miami, Florida.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 84, \"end\": 159, \"text\": \"Airways international was founded in 1979 and began operations around 1984.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 160, \"end\": 198, \"text\": \"The airline ceased operations in 1999.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 199, \"end\": 291, \"text\": \"The carrier's primary business focus was flights within southern Florida and to the Bahamas.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 292, \"end\": 344, \"text\": \"Airways International also operated charter flights.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 345, \"end\": 417, \"text\": \"In 1985, Airways began service to the Bahamas with Convair 580 aircraft.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 418, \"end\": 545, \"text\": \"Throughout its history, Airways operated a fleet of Shorts 330, Convair 580, Cessna 402, Convair 440, and Piper Aztec aircraft.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 546, \"end\": 614, \"text\": \"In 1992, the airline added the Shorts 330 to its fleet and operated.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d00\", \"start\": 615, \"end\": 649, \"text\": \"As of 1992, there were 30 aircraft\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 64, \"text\": \"Airways International was an airline based in Anchorage, Alaska.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 65, \"end\": 140, \"text\": \"Airways International was founded in 1979 and began operations around 1984.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 141, \"end\": 179, \"text\": \"The airline ceased operations in 1999.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 180, \"end\": 272, \"text\": \"The carrier's primary business focus was flights within southern Florida and to the Bahamas.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 273, \"end\": 325, \"text\": \"Airways International also operated charter flights.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 326, \"end\": 398, \"text\": \"In 1985, Airways began service to the Bahamas with Convair 580 aircraft.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 399, \"end\": 526, \"text\": \"Throughout its history, Airways operated a fleet of Shorts 330, Convair 580, Cessna 402, Convair 440, and Piper Aztec aircraft.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 527, \"end\": 595, \"text\": \"In 1992, the airline added the Shorts 330 to its fleet and operated.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d01\", \"start\": 596, \"end\": 631, \"text\": \"As of 1992, there were 30 aircraft.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 160, \"text\": \"on its own airlines , along with hotel rooms , from brick-and-mortar stores meant it had been struggling to compete with online rivals and low-budget upstarts .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"